{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Localization","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Empty\/Loading\/Error placeholders’ text — “Nothing Here,” “Loading,” “Retry,” “Something Went Wrong,” “Connection Issue” — comes from a String Catalog, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":", resolved from ScreenStates’ own bundle ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bundle.module"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than your app’s. That’s deliberate: a custom title your app passes in (see below) is never run back through localization, and a language you add to "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"your own","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" app’s catalog has no effect on these five strings — they only ever resolve against ScreenStates’ bundle. English, Spanish, French, and Russian are built in today."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Adding-a-language-to-ScreenStates","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Adding a language to ScreenStates"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a change to the package itself, not something a consuming app can do on its own — it needs a PR. Open "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":" and add a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizations"},{"type":"text","text":" entry for the new language code under each of the five string keys:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"json","code":["\"Retry\" : {","  \"comment\" : \"Title of the button that retries loading after an error.\",","  \"localizations\" : {","    \"en\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Retry\" } },","    \"de\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Wiederholen\" } }","  }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every one of the five keys needs an entry for every language — a string present in English but missing a translation elsewhere fails CI (see below). ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenStatesStrings.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s doc comments list all five keys and their English text if you’re starting from scratch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Overriding-text-per-app","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overriding text per-app"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You don’t need a new language, or a PR, to show different text than the built-in default — two options, depending on how much you want to replace:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" takes a ","type":"text"},{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directly, bypassing ","type":"text"},{"code":"Localizable.xcstrings","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entirely for that one string. Pass your own localized string (from your own app’s String Catalog, ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSLocalizedString","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whatever) instead of the default:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title: String(localized: \"No Results\"))"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has no equivalent for its title or Retry button text today — only the error’s own message is customizable, via "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For anything else — the Error placeholder’s title, the Retry button’s text, or any text at all in a shape the built-in views don’t expose a parameter for — pass a fully custom placeholder instead of the default one, via "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"empty"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loading"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":" builder closures (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"‘s equivalent. A custom placeholder can still reuse "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" so VoiceOver announces transitions with the same wording your custom text uses, instead of the default’s."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"How the default placeholders’ built-in text is localized, how to add a language, and how to show different text instead without touching ScreenStates itself.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/localization"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"title":"Localization"},"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenState","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScreenState","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The four canonical states of a screen: nothing to show yet, in flight,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"showing data, or failed."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenState","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithUIKit":{"role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drive a UIKit screen’s four states with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","title":"Getting Started with UIKit","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/gettingstartedwithuikit"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/gettingstartedwithswiftui","type":"topic","title":"Getting Started with SwiftUI","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drive a SwiftUI screen’s four states with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"article"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState/accessibilityAnnouncement":{"title":"accessibilityAnnouncement","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"accessibilityAnnouncement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate\/accessibilityannouncement","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The same text the default placeholders announce to VoiceOver for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this case, reusable by a fully custom placeholder that wants to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"announce transitions with the same wording instead of inventing its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own. "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":", since at that point a custom placeholder’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own content is what VoiceOver should read, not a transition"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"announcement."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateDisplayableError":{"title":"ScreenStateDisplayableError","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateDisplayableError"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateDisplayableError"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatedisplayableerror","abstract":[{"text":"Lets an error type supply its own user-facing message, distinct from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"localizedDescription","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — which is often a debugging string (or, for a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"Error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"CustomStringConvertible","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"LocalizedError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conformance, just the type name) rather than something to put in front","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the person using the app.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateView":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateView"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstateview","title":"ScreenStateView","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Renders the right content for a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"type":"text","text":", switching between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Empty \/ Loading \/ Data \/ Error automatically."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateView"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateStore","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" holder of a screen’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", driving both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI and UIKit consumers from a single source of truth."}],"title":"ScreenStateStore","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateStore","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates","title":"ScreenStates","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Give any screen a standard ","type":"text"},{"code":"Empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"Loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"Error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" state, usable from both UIKit and SwiftUI.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateContainerView":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateContainerView"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatecontainerview","title":"ScreenStateContainerView","abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIView"},{"text":" that swaps its content for the right placeholder based on a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"text":", mirroring ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"text":" from the SwiftUI side.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateContainerView"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateViewController":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateViewController"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"ScreenStateViewController","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateViewController","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstateviewcontroller","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIViewController"},{"type":"text","text":" base class that owns a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pinned to the view’s edges and bound to a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wrapping the boilerplate every UIKit screen using ScreenStates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise repeats in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"viewDidLoad()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/Accessibility":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/accessibility","title":"Accessibility","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything the default placeholders — and your own custom ones — get for free: VoiceOver, Reduce Motion, Increase Contrast, Dynamic Type, and stable identifiers for XCUITest."}]}}}